{{! ----- Annotations ----- }}
<section id="feature-annotations">
<h3>Annotate a document</h3>

<p>PDFs, converted office files, images and (with a converter) online text open with a toolbar
above the page. Marks are saved as you make them.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.annotation_toolbar}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.annotation_toolbar}}" width="1200" height="1067" loading="lazy"
             alt="The annotation toolbar above an essay. On the page: a green highlight with a tick, a blue highlight with a query mark, a red highlight with a numbered comment pin, and a long yellow text highlight.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The toolbar and four kinds of mark: a tick (green), a query (blue), a comment pin
    (red, numbered) and a text highlight (yellow).</figcaption>
</figure>

<h4>The tools</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Tool</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Select text</th><td>Select and copy text from the document, without marking it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Comment</th><td>Click or drag over a phrase, then type. The comment becomes a numbered pin with a card in the margin.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Highlight area</th><td>Drag a box over any part of the page, such as a chart or a diagram.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Highlight text</th><td>Drag over words to highlight them.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Strikethrough</th><td>Drag over words to strike them out.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tick, cross, query</th><td>Click or drag over a phrase to mark it <em>Good point</em>, <em>Needs correction</em> or as a question.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Select / move</th><td>Pick up a mark to move or delete it.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Shapes</th><td>Rectangle, circle, arrow or line.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Pen</th><td>Draw freehand: fine, medium or thick.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Colour</th><td>Red, yellow, green, blue or black, for the tool in use.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Undo, redo</th><td>Step back or forward through your marks.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Delete, Clear all</th><td>Remove the selected mark, or every mark on the document.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Search, document info</th><td>Find words in the document; see its details.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>Below the page: previous and next page, zoom out and in, and fit to width.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note local-unifiedgrader-help-note-tip">
    <p><strong>Ticks, crosses, queries, text highlights and comments attach to words.</strong> They
    are not free-floating stamps. Click a phrase, or drag across the words you mean.</p>
</div>

<h4>Add a comment</h4>
<ol>
    <li>Choose the <strong>Comment</strong> tool.</li>
    <li>Click a phrase, or drag across it. A small box opens, headed <em>Commenting on: …</em>.</li>
    <li>Type your comment. As you type, matching comments from your <a href="#feature-comment-library">library</a> are suggested.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Save comment</strong>, or <strong>Cancel</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<h4>What the student gets</h4>
<p>The student sees the document with your marks and the comment cards beside it. They can also
download it as a PDF with the marks printed in (see <a href="#student-feedback">Reading feedback</a>).</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Grades and feedback ----- }}
<section id="feature-grades">
<h3>Grades and feedback</h3>

<h4>Enter a grade</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Type the mark in the <strong>Grade</strong> box. The percentage appears beside it.</li>
    <li>A mark above the activity's maximum is refused.</li>
    <li>A comma works as a decimal separator: <code>3,5</code> is read as 3.5.</li>
    <li>Activities graded on a scale show a menu in place of the box.</li>
    <li>Activities with no grade show a <strong>Mark as graded</strong> switch.</li>
</ul>

<details class="local-unifiedgrader-help-details">
    <summary>Clear or reset a grade</summary>
    <div>
        <p>Type <code>-</code> in the grade box and save to return the student to <em>no grade</em>.
        Feedback, annotations and the submission are kept.</p>
        <p>Type <code>--</code> for a full reset. As well as clearing the grade, it removes an empty
        submission record that marking may have created (real submissions are never removed), and
        it releases a gradebook override that was holding the old value. On a rated forum it
        withdraws your own ratings for that student.</p>
    </div>
</details>

<div id="feature-feedback">
<h4>Write feedback</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Type in <strong>Overall Feedback</strong>. You can format text and add images. If your site
        has an audio or video recorder for the editor, you can record feedback too.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Save feedback</strong>. Saved feedback is shown read-only, marked
        <em>Feedback (saved)</em>, with <strong>Edit</strong> and <strong>Delete</strong> buttons.</li>
    <li><strong>Feedback files</strong> opens an upload area, when the assignment allows feedback files.</li>
    <li>The speech-bubble icon beside the heading opens the <a href="#feature-comment-library">comment library</a>.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>

{{! ----- Rubrics and marking guides ----- }}
<section id="feature-rubrics">
<h3>Rubrics and marking guides</h3>

<p>When the activity uses advanced grading, the rubric or marking guide appears in the marking
panel and fills the grade for you. The badge beside the heading shows the running total.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.rubric_panel}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.rubric_panel}}" width="900" height="429" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A rubric with two criteria, Argument and Use of sources. Each has three levels worth 0, 5 and 10 points; one level per criterion is selected. The heading shows 15 points.">
        </a>
        <figcaption><strong>Rubric:</strong> click one level for each criterion. The comment icon
        under a criterion adds a remark.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.marking_guide_panel}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.marking_guide_panel}}" width="900" height="579" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A marking guide with two criteria. Each shows its maximum, a note for graders, a score box and a remark. The heading shows 31 out of 40.">
        </a>
        <figcaption><strong>Marking guide:</strong> type a score and a remark for each criterion.
        The note for graders and the maximum are shown.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>A marking-guide score below zero or above the criterion's maximum is flagged in red, and nothing is saved until it is corrected.</li>
    <li>The icon beside a remark opens the <a href="#feature-comment-library">comment library</a>. In a marking guide, typing in a remark also suggests matching library comments.</li>
    <li>Ranged rubrics are shown too, on sites that have the rubric ranges grading method installed.</li>
</ul>

<h4>Change the calculated grade</h4>
<p>If your administrator allows it, you can type over the grade the rubric or guide calculated. An
<strong>Overridden</strong> badge then shows the calculated total with a
<strong>Reset to rubric total</strong> link. If the setting is off, the grade always comes from the criteria.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Comment library ----- }}
<section id="feature-comment-library">
<h3>Comment library</h3>

<p>Keep the comments you write often and reuse them in feedback, rubric remarks, annotations and
recording comments.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.comment_library}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.comment_library}}" width="1200" height="955" loading="lazy"
             alt="The Comment Library popout over the feedback area: a tag filter set to All, four saved comments, a Quick add comment box with a plus button, and a Manage Library link.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The library popout: click a comment to insert it, type in <strong>Quick add</strong>
    to save a new one, or open <strong>Manage Library</strong>.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h4>Use it</h4>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Insert:</strong> open the popout with the speech-bubble icon and click a comment.</li>
    <li><strong>Filter:</strong> click a tag at the top of the popout.</li>
    <li><strong>Quick add:</strong> type a comment in the box at the bottom and press <strong>+</strong>. It is saved for the current course.</li>
    <li><strong>Manage Library:</strong> edit and delete comments, tag them, search them, and share them.</li>
</ul>

<h4>Where a comment appears</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Kind</th><th scope="col">Who sees it, and where</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Course comment</th><td>You, in every course with the same course code (for example each term's offering of the same course).</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Universal</th><td>You, in every course. Tick <em>Universal</em> when adding or editing the comment.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Shared</th><td>Other teachers, who can copy it into their own library.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">System default <i class="fa fa-star" aria-hidden="true"></i></th><td>Every teacher, in every course. Read-only, and maintained by the site.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<h4>Suggest a comment for everyone</h4>
<p>In <strong>Manage Library</strong>, the star on one of your comments suggests it as a system
default. Depending on the site's setting it is added at once, or waits for approval and shows
<em>Pending review</em> (then <em>Rejected</em>, with the reason, if it is declined).</p>

<h4>Tidy or export your library</h4>
<p><strong>Organise my comment library</strong> lists your comments by the course they are filed
under, lets you move them, and has <strong>Export my library (CSV)</strong>.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Notes and messages ----- }}
<section id="feature-notes">
<h3>Notes and messages</h3>

<h4>Teacher notes</h4>
<p>Notes are for teachers only. Students never see them. Use them for handovers between markers
and reminders to follow up.</p>
<ol>
    <li>Press <strong>Add note</strong> in the <strong>Teacher notes</strong> card.</li>
    <li>Type the note and press <strong>Save note</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<p>Each note shows who wrote it and when. The <strong>&times;</strong> on a note deletes it.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.teacher_notes}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.teacher_notes}}" width="760" height="323" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Teacher notes card with a text box holding a note, and Save note and Cancel buttons.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Writing a note.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.teacher_notes_saved}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.teacher_notes_saved}}" width="760" height="211" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The saved note, showing the teacher's name, the date and time, and a delete cross.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The saved note, with its author and time.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<div id="feature-submission-comments">
<h4>Submission comments</h4>
<p>The speech-bubble icon beside the status badge opens a message thread with the student about
this piece of work. Type a message and send it. The student is notified and can reply from the
activity page or their feedback page, before and after grading.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.submission_comments}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.submission_comments}}" width="1200" height="614" loading="lazy"
             alt="The Submission comments popout under the header, empty, with a Type a message box and a send button.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The submission comments thread opens from the icon beside the status badge.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>

{{! ----- Post grades ----- }}
<section id="feature-post-grades">
<h3>Post grades <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h3>

<p>Students see a grade and its feedback only once it is <em>posted</em>. The control in the
header shows the current state (<em>Grades posted</em>, <em>Grades hidden</em>, or a count such as
<em>1 of 4 posted</em>) and opens the menu.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.post_grades_menu}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.post_grades_menu}}" width="1200" height="614" loading="lazy"
             alt="The post-grades menu open under a control reading 1 of 4 posted. It lists Post this student, Hide this student, Post the whole class, Hide the whole class, and a Post on a date section with a scope menu, a date box and a Schedule button.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>The post-grades menu on an assignment.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">To…</th><th scope="col">Choose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Show or hide the open student's grade</th><td><strong>Post this student</strong> / <strong>Hide this student</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Show or hide everyone's grades</th><td><strong>Post the whole class</strong> / <strong>Hide the whole class</strong></td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Show or hide the groups you are filtering by</th><td>The <strong>Post</strong> / <strong>Hide</strong> entries named after those groups (shown when a group is selected)</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Post later</th><td><strong>Post on a date</strong>: pick <em>The whole class</em>, <em>This student</em> or <em>The groups in view</em>, set a date and time in the future, press <strong>Schedule</strong></td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>Posting and hiding always ask you to confirm.</li>
    <li>The eye in each row of the student list shows who is posted.</li>
    <li>A grade you save later for a student who is not posted stays hidden.</li>
    <li>In a separate-groups activity, a teacher who cannot see all groups can post their own groups, not the whole class.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-small">
    <a href="{{img.partial_post}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.partial_post}}" width="700" height="132" loading="lazy"
             alt="The header control reading 1 of 4 posted, beside the Friction feedback menu set to Site default.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>A partly posted class.</figcaption>
</figure>

<h4>Quizzes</h4>
<p>The control appears on a quiz only when the administrator has enabled it. It then offers the
four post and hide actions. There is no <em>Post on a date</em> for quizzes.</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>The whole class:</strong> switches on <em>Marks</em>, <em>Maximum mark</em> and
        <em>Overall feedback</em> in the quiz's review options, for <em>Later, while the quiz is still
        open</em> and <em>After the quiz is closed</em>. Hiding switches them off. No other review option is touched.</li>
    <li><strong>One student or a group:</strong> shows the grade in the gradebook and in the Unified
        Grader feedback. The quiz's own review page keeps following the review options.</li>
    <li>Whether students can open their attempt at all still depends on <em>The attempt</em> in the review options.</li>
</ul>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-narrow">
    <a href="{{img.quiz_post_grades}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.quiz_post_grades}}" width="1200" height="614" loading="lazy"
             alt="The post-grades menu on a quiz: Post this student, Hide this student, Post the whole class, Hide the whole class. There is no date section.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>On a quiz the menu has the four post and hide actions only.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>

{{! ----- Friction feedback (teacher side) ----- }}
<section id="feature-friction">
<h3>Friction Feedback <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h3>

<p>Friction Feedback holds the mark back until the student has read the feedback. You post the
grade as usual. The student reads the feedback one part at a time, confirms each part, and then
sees the mark. <a href="#student-friction">See what the student sees</a>.</p>

<h4>Switch it on or off for an activity</h4>
<p>Use the <strong>Friction feedback</strong> menu in the header:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Site default</strong>: follow the site setting (off unless your administrator turned it on).</li>
    <li><strong>On for this activity</strong> or <strong>Off for this activity</strong>: decide here, whatever the site says.</li>
</ul>

<h4>What happens when you post</h4>
<ul>
    <li>The walk starts for a student when their grade is posted after having been hidden. They are told their feedback is ready.</li>
    <li>There is one step per rubric criterion, marking-guide criterion or manually marked quiz question, and one for the overall feedback. Points are not shown during the walk.</li>
    <li>You still see the grade as posted. For the student, the mark stays hidden in the gradebook until they finish.</li>
    <li>If you change the mark afterwards, the walk starts again.</li>
    <li>A student who never opens the feedback still gets their mark: it is released automatically a set number of days after posting, or before the course ends, whichever comes first (21 and 14 days unless your administrator changed them).</li>
</ul>
</section>

{{! ----- Penalties ----- }}
<section id="feature-penalties">
<h3>Penalties</h3>

<h4>Late penalties <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h4>
<p>Late penalties work the same way for assignments, forums and quizzes. Two things must be in place:</p>
<ol>
    <li>The activity has <strong>Apply late penalties</strong> ticked, in the <em>Late penalties</em> section of its settings.</li>
    <li>Your site has penalty rules, set by the administrator or for the course in Moodle's grade penalty settings (for example 10% for each day late).</li>
</ol>

<p>When a submission is late, the marking panel shows:</p>
<ul>
    <li>a banner with the exact lateness, such as <em>Late: 1 day 23 hours</em>;</li>
    <li>a red badge with the penalty, such as <em>&minus;10% 2 day(s) late</em>;</li>
    <li>once a grade is entered, <em>Final grade after penalties: 50 / 100 (50%)</em>.</li>
</ul>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.late_penalty_panel}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.late_penalty_panel}}" width="760" height="294" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A late banner above the grade card. The grade is 60 out of 100, a red badge reads minus 10 percent, 2 days late, and below it: Final grade after penalties: 50 out of 100, 50 percent.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>A late assignment: the banner, the penalty badge and the final grade.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.penalties_popout}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.penalties_popout}}" width="1200" height="818" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Penalties popout: Word count with 5, 10, 15, 20 percent and Custom buttons; Other with a label box and the same buttons; and Active penalties listing the late penalty.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The <strong>Penalties</strong> popout: add a penalty, and see those in force.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note">
    <p><strong>Part days count as whole days.</strong> The penalty counts each day that has
    started. A submission 1 day and 23 hours late is in its second day, so it is charged for
    2 days.</p>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>The grade you type is kept as you typed it. The gradebook records the deduction beside it and shows the reduced grade to the student.</li>
    <li>The student sees the working: their feedback page and feedback PDF list the mark you awarded, each penalty with its reason and the marks it cost, and the final grade. See <a href="#student-messages">what students see</a>. For a penalty of your own, the label you type (for example <em>Plagiarism</em>) is the reason shown, so choose it for the student to read.</li>
    <li>You cannot edit a late penalty by hand. To excuse a student, <a href="#feature-overrides">extend their due date</a>. The penalty is recalculated at once.</li>
    <li>The penalty is also applied when someone grades on Moodle's own pages, and when a quiz is regraded.</li>
</ul>

<h4>Other penalties</h4>
<p>Press <strong>Penalties</strong> beside the grade to deduct for something else:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Word count</strong>, or <strong>Other</strong> with your own label of up to 15 characters.</li>
    <li>Choose 5%, 10%, 15%, 20% or <strong>Custom</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Active penalties</strong> lists what applies to this student. Remove one you added from there.</li>
</ul>
<p>These penalties are not offered when the activity is graded on a scale. A forum graded by post
ratings is offered them only when its ratings are points combined by average or sum (see
<a href="#integration-forum">Forums</a>).</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Dates and extensions ----- }}
<section id="feature-overrides">
<h3>Dates and extensions <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h3>

<p>Give one student different dates without leaving the grader. Open the status badge menu and
choose <strong>Dates &amp; extensions</strong>. It is available for assignments, quizzes and
forums with whole-forum grading.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.dates_extensions}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.dates_extensions}}" width="1200" height="968" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Dates and extensions dialogue for an assignment. A green line says Submitted on time. Below: Extend the due date with plus 1 day, plus 2 days, plus 3 days and plus 1 week buttons and a date box; then a table of Submissions open, Due date and Cut-off date with the class default and this student's value; then Remove all overrides, Cancel and Save.">
        </a>
        <figcaption><strong>Assignment:</strong> Submissions open, Due date, Cut-off date.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.quiz_dates_extensions}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.quiz_dates_extensions}}" width="1200" height="1118" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Dates and extensions dialogue for a quiz. An amber line says Submitted late: minus 10 percent late penalty. The table lists Opens, Due date, Closes, Time limit and Attempts allowed.">
        </a>
        <figcaption><strong>Quiz:</strong> Opens, Due date, Closes, Time limit, Attempts allowed.
        The status line shows the penalty this student carries now.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<h4>Give an extension</h4>
<ol>
    <li>Read the status line at the top: on time, or late with the penalty it carries.</li>
    <li>Under <strong>Extend the due date</strong>, press a preset (<em>+1 day</em>, <em>+2 days</em>,
        <em>+3 days</em>, <em>+1 week</em> unless your site changed them) or pick a date.</li>
    <li>The status line updates to show the result, for example <em>On time with this extension</em>.</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Save</strong>. Nothing changes until you do.</li>
</ol>

<h4>Change another date or limit</h4>
<ul>
    <li>The table shows each setting with the <em>class default</em> and <em>this student's</em> value.</li>
    <li><strong>Change</strong> opens the value for editing in its row. <strong>Reset</strong> puts the class default back.</li>
    <li>If an extension passes the cut-off or closing date, that date moves with it, and its row says so.</li>
    <li><strong>Remove all overrides</strong> returns the student to the class dates.</li>
</ul>

<h4>Forums: extensions past the cut-off date</h4>
<p>Moodle cannot set a forum's cut-off date for one student, so the cut-off row keeps the class
date. An extension that runs past it still works: the student is given a temporary role in that
forum only, <em>Forum extension (Unified Grader)</em>, which lets them post until their extension
ends. Nobody else is affected. The role goes when the extension ends (checked every 15 minutes), or
straight away if you remove the extension or bring it back before the cut-off. Moodle's own notice
that the cut-off has passed still shows on the forum page, but the student's <em>Reply</em> links
are there and their posts are accepted.</p>
<p>A forum graded by post ratings has <strong>Dates &amp; extensions</strong> too, for this
reason. If its ratings are points combined by average or sum, the dialogue shows the late penalty
as it does for any forum. Otherwise it takes no late penalty and the dialogue says so.</p>
<p>The footer shows how many changes are waiting to be saved.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Academic integrity ----- }}
<section id="feature-referral">
<h3>Academic integrity</h3>

<h4>Plagiarism results</h4>
<p>If your site uses a plagiarism plugin, its result for each file or text appears in a
<strong>Plagiarism</strong> card at the top of the marking panel. The grader shows whatever that
plugin returns: scores, colours and links to the full report are the plugin's own. The examples
here come from one such plugin; yours may look different.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots local-unifiedgrader-help-shots-3">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.plagiarism_high}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.plagiarism_high}}" width="760" height="295" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A Plagiarism card for sower-essay.pdf: AI content score 0 percent, plagiarism score 98 percent, and a Report academic impropriety button.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>A file with a 98% similarity score.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.plagiarism_copied}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.plagiarism_copied}}" width="760" height="294" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A Plagiarism card for online text: AI content score 0 percent, plagiarism score 100 percent.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Online text that was copied in full.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.plagiarism_ai}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.plagiarism_ai}}" width="760" height="294" loading="lazy"
                 alt="A Plagiarism card for online text: AI content score 100 percent, plagiarism score 0 percent.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>Online text flagged as AI-written.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<h4>Refer a submission for review</h4>
<p>When work needs an integrity review, flag it from the marking panel. Flagging records the
referral and pauses the grading-turnaround clock in reports that measure it, so the wait for a
decision is not counted against you.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Your site</th><th scope="col">The button</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Has a report form, and a plagiarism card is showing</th>
            <td><strong>Report academic impropriety</strong>, in the plagiarism card</td>
            <td>Asks you to confirm, flags the submission, and opens your institution's report form in a new tab with the student, course and activity filled in.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <th scope="row">Anything else</th>
            <td><strong>Refer for integrity review</strong>, in the grade card</td>
            <td>Lets you add an optional note for the reviewers, then flags the submission.</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<p>A flagged submission shows <strong>Referred for integrity review</strong>. When the review is
over, press <strong>Mark resolved</strong>.</p>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot local-unifiedgrader-help-shot-small">
    <a href="{{img.referred}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.referred}}" width="760" height="289" loading="lazy"
             alt="A Plagiarism card with a red badge reading Referred for integrity review and a Mark resolved link.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>After flagging: the referral badge and <strong>Mark resolved</strong>.</figcaption>
</figure>

<p>The button needs the <code>local/unifiedgrader:refer</code> permission, which editing teachers
and managers have by default.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Proctoring ----- }}
<section id="feature-proctoring">
<span id="plugin-smowl" class="local-unifiedgrader-help-anchor"></span>
<h3>Proctoring results <span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-new">New in 3.0</span></h3>

<p>If your institution proctors quizzes, the grader shows how closely each attempt deserves a
look. It does not judge the student: it points you to the evidence held by the proctoring service.</p>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-note">
    <p><strong>The example is from SMOWL.</strong> What you see depends on your proctoring service:
    the findings listed, their wording, and the report the link opens all differ between Quilgo,
    ProctorLink, AutoProctor and SMOWL.</p>
</div>

<figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
    <a href="{{img.proctoring_smowl}}" data-action="help-zoom">
        <img src="{{img.proctoring_smowl}}" width="1600" height="909" loading="lazy"
             alt="A proctored quiz in the grader. Above the grade, a Proctoring card reads High review priority, provisional, and lists camera, audio and computer monitoring findings with an Open SMOWL report button.">
    </a>
    <figcaption>A proctored quiz: the <strong>Proctoring</strong> card sits above the grade.</figcaption>
</figure>

<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shots">
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.proctoring_card}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.proctoring_card}}" width="760" height="341" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The Proctoring card: High review priority. Provisional: some of the evidence is still being reviewed. Front camera: no incidents. Audio: no incidents. Computer monitoring: incidents, with three listed. An Open SMOWL report button and the time of the last update.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The card: the priority, the findings behind it, a link to the evidence, and a refresh button.</figcaption>
    </figure>
    <figure class="local-unifiedgrader-help-shot">
        <a href="{{img.proctoring_navigator}}" data-action="help-zoom">
            <img src="{{img.proctoring_navigator}}" width="560" height="444" loading="lazy"
                 alt="The student list on a proctored quiz. One student has a hollow red circle beside their name.">
        </a>
        <figcaption>The marker in the student list. Hollow means the review is not finished.</figcaption>
    </figure>
</div>

<h4>Read the marker</h4>
<div class="local-unifiedgrader-help-table">
<table class="table-reboot">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Marker</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-dot local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-red"></span> Red</th><td>High review priority. Look at the evidence.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-dot local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-yellow"></span> Yellow</th><td>Medium review priority.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-dot local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-green"></span> Green</th><td>Low review priority. Shown only once the service has finished its review.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-dot local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-red local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-hollow"></span> Hollow red or yellow</th><td>Provisional. Something has been reported already and the review is still going, so more may follow.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><span class="local-unifiedgrader-help-dot local-unifiedgrader-help-dot-grey"></span> Grey, <em>Awaiting review</em></th><td>Nothing reported so far, and the review is not finished. This is not an all-clear.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
</div>

<ul>
    <li>The colour is a guide to where to look first. It can differ from what the service's own report suggests.</li>
    <li>Where the service keeps a result per attempt, the card follows the attempt selector and the list shows the student's worst attempt.</li>
    <li>Results are kept for fifteen minutes. The refresh button on the card asks the service again.</li>
    <li><em>SMOWL is not active on this quiz</em> means the course uses SMOWL but this quiz was not switched on there, so attempts were not monitored.</li>
    <li>You see proctoring results only with the <code>local/unifiedgrader:viewproctoring</code> permission. The link to the report also needs the proctoring plugin's own permission.</li>
</ul>
<p>Administrators: see <a href="#admin-proctoring">Proctoring setup</a> for how each service decides the colour.</p>
</section>

{{! ----- Saving and groups ----- }}
<section id="feature-autosave">
<h3>Saving and groups</h3>

<h4>Saving</h4>
<ul>
    <li>Grades, rubric choices, remarks and annotations save by themselves shortly after you leave a field. <strong>Save feedback</strong> saves at once.</li>
    <li>The header shows the state: <em>All changes saved</em>, or a warning while something is unsaved.</li>
    <li>Moving to another student saves first.</li>
    <li>If the connection drops, your work is kept in the browser, the header shows <em>Offline — saved locally</em>, and it is sent when the connection returns. If you reload before that, the grader offers to <strong>Restore</strong> the unsaved changes.</li>
</ul>

<div id="feature-groups">
<h4>Groups</h4>
<ul>
    <li>In an activity that uses groups, a group selector appears in the student list. Tick one or more groups, <em>All my groups</em>, or <em>All groups</em>.</li>
    <li>It opens on your own group or groups, and remembers your choice for each activity.</li>
    <li>The groups you select are also the groups the <a href="#feature-post-grades">post-grades menu</a> offers to post or hide.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
